# Runs before every `git commit`. Fast enough to not annoy — the unit
# suite completes in ~1s and lint in ~5s. Skips the App smoke test
# (which pulls in the entire RN module graph) via `test:unit`.
#
# Lint currently allows warnings through (pre-existing inline-style
# / no-shadow noise). Only ESLint *errors* block the commit. Bump this
# to `npm run lint -- --max-warnings 0` once the warning backlog is
# cleaned up.
#
# To bypass in an emergency (do not make a habit of it):
#   git commit --no-verify

npm run test:unit && npm run lint
